["Provides access to documentation search for a specific hosting and deployment platform and tools to manage its projects and deployments, including listing projects, deployments, build logs, and creating temporary authenticated share URLs or fetching protected deployment URLs. Also supports deploying the current project through the platform’s API, listing teams, and checking domain availability and pricing.

MCP server instructions: Vercel MCP provides over 200 tools. Capabilities:
Deployments: builds, status/logs/files, aliases, promotions, rollbacks, rolling releases and sharing/access.
Insights: runtime errors/logs, Web Analytics, observability metrics, usage/billing and agent run traces.
Configuration: projects, accounts/teams/access groups, environment variables, domains/pricing/registration, DNS/TLS, routes/redirects, microfrontends, feature flags, Blob stores and Global Config (Edge Config).
Platform: cache artifacts/invalidatio...

List deployments under the authenticated user or team. If a deployment hasn't finished uploading (is incomplete), the `url` property will have a value of `null`.

CLI fallback on MCP failure (partial): vercel --scope {teamSlugOrId} list {projectName}. Fill placeholders from inputs. This tool is part of plugin `Vercel`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__vercel_list_deployments(args: {
  // Name of the deployment.
  app?: string;
  // Filter deployments based on the branch name
  branch?: string;
  // Gets the deployment created after this Date timestamp. (default: current time)
  from?: number;
  // Maximum number of deployments to list from a request.
  limit?: number;
  // Filter deployments from the given ID or name.
  projectId?: string;
  // Filter deployments from the given project IDs. Cannot be used when projectId is specified.
  projectIds?: Array<string>;
  // Filter deployments based on their rollback candidacy
  rollbackCandidate?: boolean;
  // Filter deployments based on the SHA
  sha?: string;
  // Get Deployments created after this JavaScript timestamp.
  since?: number;
  // Team slug to use for this operation. Use instead of teamId.
  slug?: string;
  // Filter deployments based on their state (`BUILDING`, `ERROR`, `INITIALIZING`, `QUEUED`, `READY`, `CANCELED`, `BLOCKED`)
  state?: string;
  // Filter deployments based on the environment.
  target?: string;
  // Team ID to use for this operation.
  teamId?: string;
  // Gets the deployment created before this Date timestamp. (default: current time)
  to?: number;
  // Get Deployments created before this JavaScript timestamp.
  until?: number;
  // Filter out deployments based on users who have created the deployment.
  users?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```","Provides access to documentation search for a specific hosting and deployment platform and tools to manage its projects and deployments, including listing projects, deployments, build logs, and creating temporary authenticated share URLs or fetching protected deployment URLs. Also supports deploying the current project through the platform’s API, listing teams, and checking domain availability and pricing.

